<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- The strip along the bottom of the player that never accepts a touch,
         not even while the overlay has been lifted.

         What it covers is everything below YouTube's seek bar, less a margin
         left reachable for a thumb. The embed draws its control row inset from
         the bottom edge, so under the bar there is a band that belongs to
         nothing useful — and a scrub that drifts downward off the bar lands
         there, on whatever the player puts under it, or on the system's
         back/home gesture.

         This is only the STARTING value, and the only number about the player's
         geometry left in the app. The player is a cross-origin iframe, so its
         DOM cannot be read and there is no way to ask where the bar is — but
         there is a way to look, and PlayerActivity does: on the first pause it
         draws the bottom of the player and finds the seek bar in the pixels,
         then sets this height from what it found, margin included. Chrome.kt
         takes its scale from the bar's own drawn thickness, so there is no dp
         figure for YouTube's chrome anywhere and no density to convert with.

         What is left here is the fallback for before that has happened and for
         when it fails. Erring small on purpose: too tall and it eats the seek
         bar, which is the one control the reveal exists to reach. -->
    <dimen name="player_bottom_block">16dp</dimen>

</resources>
